    "analysis": "MemPalace is a local-first AI memory system that stores conversation history and project files verbatim and retrieves them by semantic search, organized into wings (people/projects), rooms (topics) and drawers (content). It provides a Python CLI, an MCP server, and plugins, skills and hooks for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and Antigravity, with a pluggable vector backend (ChromaDB default, plus SQLite exact, Rust, Milvus, Qdrant, pgvector). It reports 96.6% R@5 on LongMemEval with no LLM or API calls and targets developers who want persistent memory across agent sessions.",
